 MAIN-9407, MAIN-9410"],["Alec Patterson","Developer","2","MM-270, MS-2255"],["Amish Shah","Developer","2","MM-147, MM-300"],["Eric Stempert","Developer","2","MAIN-7842, MAIN-9577"],["Frank Hrach IV","Developer","2","MAIN-8570, MAIN-9656"],["Holland Cooper","Jr Dev","2","MAIN-9420, MAIN-9796"],["Seth Burleson","Developer","2","PNP-4748, PNP-4785"],["Alex Secor","Jr Dev","1","MAIN-9401"],["Anastasia Holt","Jr Dev","1","MAIN-9750"],["Brittany Grizzard","QA","1","MAIN-8432"],["Christian Cox","Developer","1","MAIN-9623"],["Colin Knecht","Developer","1","MAIN-9454"],["Dustin White","Jr Dev","1","CL-1379"],["Kevin Nichols","Developer","1","PNP-4777"],["Michael Paserba Tessari","Developer","1","MAIN-9638"],["Mike Thompson","Developer","1","MAIN-7837"],["Quinn James","Developer","1","MAIN-9767"],["Sarah Carlough","QA","1","TIN-475"],["Tony Young","Jr Dev","1","MAIN-8703"]]},"legend":["MARS Dev Team Weekly Report — Legend & Methodology","Report week: Monday 9/7/2026 – Friday 9/11/2026 | Generated per MARS_Reporting_Spec_v4.md | Run type: standard weekly run (first weekly run of September 2026)","This run at a glance","• Month-to-Date tab: SKIPPED this run. Per the Standing Rules, the [Month] MTD tab is only built on the final weekly run of the month. This is the first weekly run of September, so this workbook goes straight from Weekly Summary to Dev Closes, as specified.","• Holiday: Monday 9/7/2026 is a full company closure per the Holiday Schedule (0 expected hours for everyone). No one logged time that day. Tuesday–Friday were normal workdays; no half-days fell in this window.","• Dev Closes / QA Closes MTD window: since this is the first week of September, the MTD window (Sept 1–13) and this report week (Sept 7–13) cover the same underlying activity — the changelog shows zero qualifying closures dated before Sept 7, so the two windows produce identical results this run.","• Unattributed Dev Closes this run: 113 of 249 tickets closed (45.4%). This is slightly above the ~35–45% range noted in the spec as a known, currently-unexplained characteristic of this data source — flagged here per standing instructions, not treated as a new problem.","Erin Terre (Staff Engineer) and Halina Bobrykava (Senior Dev) are included in every tab on this workbook like any other roster member — see the \"Bounce/Low-Volume Flag role eligibility\" note below for how their rows are handled where the spec restricts a flag to certain roles.","Input files used for this run","1. Full-week worklog: worklogs_07_09_2026_13_09_2026.xlsx (\"Data\" sheet)","2. Issue History changelog: Issue_History_week_of_2026_09_07.xlsx (full lifecycle history, back to May 2024, 2,652 rows / 620 distinct tickets — used for both bounce and dev-owner attribution)","3. Timecard PTO: PTO_week_of_2026_09_07.xlsx — no separate \"Status\" column present, so every row was treated as already-approved, per spec.","4. Employee roster: Employees__Hrs_per_Week_Expected.xlsx (Project Knowledge, 52 employees)","Exclusions applied","• Non-roster names ignored from the worklog (logged time, but not on the roster): Beez Khumin-taylor, Bricen Bennett, pam.barwick.","• Non-roster names ignored from the PTO file: Jake Hennett, Katie Wiggins, Michael Rast.","• Excluded ticket prefixes (customer-facing): 10 worklog rows excluded, all under the PSC- prefix (e.g. PSC-73654 etc.); no PS- or MSP- rows were present this run.","• Batch-log artifacts (single entry >12h on one ticket/one day): none found this run.","• No person's hours summed to an implausible daily total across many small tickets this week (the highest was Michael Tessari at ~10.7h across 3 tickets on Thursday, which is a long day but not implausible) — nothing met the bar for a Notes flag on this front.","• Name normalization table was applied exactly as specified (Aleisha→Aleisha DeYoung, Nicholas Haile→Nick Haile, Lee Ann Madar→Lee Ann Robinson, Jonathan Collins→JC Collins, Allen Mcafee→Allen McAfee, alec.patterson→Alec Patterson, david.swanson→David Swanson, Michael Tessari→Michael Paserba Tessari, Frank Hrach→Frank Hrach IV). Beez Khumin-taylor is confirmed not on the roster and excluded per spec.","• Two tickets (CL-1343, CL-1341) transitioned directly To Do → Closed (a different terminal status from \"Done\"). The spec's Dev-owner/Dev Closes rules are written specifically around the \"Done\" status, so these were not counted as Dev Closes credit events. Flagged here as an assumption, not a silent decision.","PTO handling this run","Every timecard row (PTO, Sick (PTO), Late In, Early Out, etc.) counted as time away from work regardless of label, per spec. Multi-day/multi-hour requests were spread across consecutive weekdays at 7.5h/day starting at Request Start (skipping weekends). Two requests (JC Collins' 45h PTO starting 9/11, and Lavona Williams' 15h PTO starting 9/11) extend past this report week into the week of 9/14 — only the portion landing in this report week (9/11) is reflected here; the rest will land in next week's run.","Full-PTO-day vs. partial-PTO-day status used the combined (logged + PTO) ≥ 7.5h test, evaluated only on days with an actual PTO entry, exactly as specified. Where combined hours reached a full day, the cell shows \"PTO\" (green) and that day's logged hours are intentionally not separately added to Wk Total, per spec's stated intended behavior — this affected several people this week (e.g. Seth Burleson logged 6.0h on Friday but had 2.0h of Late-In PTO that day, so the combined 8.0h marks the whole day as PTO and the 6.0h is not separately counted).","Bounce-back rules & this run's numbers","Bounce Flag / bounce-rate tracking applies only to Developer, Jr Dev, and Senior Dev roles per spec. QA, Staff Engineer, Data Engineer, and Other show \"n/a\" in the Bounce Flag column. However, the underlying Bounced count and Bounce Rate % (n/m) columns are shown as real, computed numbers for every role (not blanked out) so that nobody's row is silently hidden — this includes Erin Terre (Staff Engineer), who was legitimately the dev-owner on one ticket (MAIN-9703) that bounced this week. Her Bounce Flag still reads \"n/a\" because the spec doesn't define HIGH/WATCH/OK bands for her role, not because her activity was excluded.","58 raw testing→dev transitions were found in the full changelog history (all of them, as it happens, dated within this report week — the changelog's status churn is heavily concentrated in the current sprint). Of those, 8 were excluded as self-moves (actor was the credited dev-owner) and 1 was excluded as an instant reversal (same-minute as the preceding forward-into-testing move). The remainder were credited to the ticket's dev-owner (never the literal actor on the reversal row), using the persisted event-1 owner and the tight-split-row walk-back rule exactly as specified.","Dev-owner attribution & Dev Closes","Dev-owner credit locks in at a real hand-off from a dev-stage status into testing/publish-staging (event 1), or — only if event 1 never happened for that ticket — a direct dev-status→Done transition (event 2). Once established via event 1, the dev-owner persists for that ticket's eventual close regardless of what precedes the Done row. The tight (≤60s) split-row walk-back was applied so that a same-second QA hand-off pattern (reassign, then status change) credits the outgoing developer, not the incoming QA/PM name. Reopened-and-reclosed tickets within the window were de-duplicated, keeping the most recent closure's credit (this occurred once this run, on MAIN-8919).","Tickets left unattributed (113 this run) fall into the documented residual-gap categories: the changelog history starts mid-flow already inside a testing/publish status with no dev-status row to anchor on, the credited person resolves to a real non-roster name (QA/PM/other-team), or the credited slot is literally Unassigned at the hand-off/closure moment. Under-counting is intentional and preferred over mis-crediting a QA tester or release coordinator with a developer's work.","QA Closes limitation","QA Closes only captures QA testing time logged on a dedicated sub-ticket matching the exact pattern \"SUBKEY: PARENTKEY | QA\" whose parent ticket reached Done within the MTD window; QA time logged directly on a parent ticket isn't visible to this method. This run found exactly one candidate — Nherissa Dagal's time on MAIN-9312, a QA sub-ticket for parent MAIN-6275 — but MAIN-6275 has not reached Done as of this run (it was last seen at \"Awaiting Publish to Live\"), so it does not qualify. The QA Closes tab is therefore empty this week; this is expected given the data, not an error.","Flag columns — role eligibility recap","• Bounce Flag: Developer, Jr Dev, Senior Dev only. n/a for QA, Staff Engineer, Data Engineer, Other.","• Low Volume Flag: Developer, Jr Dev, QA only. n/a for Senior Dev, Staff Engineer, Data Engineer, Other. Target T = FLOOR(1.5 × full-day-equivalents worked this period); this week's holiday reduces the baseline full-day-equivalent count below the usual full-week value of 5, so T is lower than a typical non-holiday week even for someone with perfect attendance (T=6 rather than T=7 for a full 5-day week with no time off).","• Low Hours Flag: applies to every role, compares Wk Total against the PTO/holiday-adjusted prorated period target. RED < 50%, ORANGE 50–70%, OK > 70%.","Row sort order on Weekly Summary: Bounce Flag severity (HIGH → WATCH → OK/n/a), then Low Hours Flag severity (RED → ORANGE → OK), then hours logged (Wk Total) descending within each group.","Formatting key","Dark-blue header fill, white bold text = column headers. Green = full PTO day. Gray = company holiday. Red fill/dark-red text = RED tier (Low Volume/Low Hours flags, and daily cell shading below 50% of that day's goal). Orange fill/dark-orange text = ORANGE tier (50–70% of goal). Peach fill = Bounce Flag HIGH. Pale-yellow fill = Bounce Flag WATCH. A trailing * on a daily hours cell marks a partial-PTO day (see Notes for that row).","Formula vs. script-computed values","Wk Total, Bounce Rate % (n/m), Bounce Flag, Low Volume Flag, and Low Hours Flag are live Excel formulas that recalculate from other cells in the same row (including hidden helper columns S–W on Weekly Summary: Bounce Denominator, Bounce Rate (numeric), Prorated Goal, Low-Hours Ratio, and Low-Volume Target T). Tickets Worked, Bounced, and Dev Closes counts, along with the daily Mon–Fri hour values themselves, are computed by script from the worklog/PTO/changelog state-machine logic described above — that sequential logic (bounce credit, dev-owner walk-back, PTO spreading) can't reasonably be expressed as in-sheet spreadsheet formulas, so those specific inputs are hardcoded values, documented here per the reporting methodology's own instructions.","Ad Hoc Report reminder","The Cross-Week Flag Summary (a separate, on-request report built from multiple weeks' Weekly Summary tabs) was not requested or built this run."],"meta":{"expectedProrated":1124.2,"expectedProratedByRole":{"Data/Other":50,"Developer":494.8,"Jr Dev":268,"QA":277.2,"Senior/Staff":34.2}},"mtd":{"headers":[],"notes":[],"rows":[]},"qaCloses":{"headers":["QA","Closed Count","Ticket Keys (MTD)"],"note":"Limitation: this tab only captures QA testing logged on a dedicated sub-ticket matching the pattern 'SUBKEY: PARENTKEY | QA' (e.g. MAIN-8897: MAIN-8803 | QA), whose parent ticket reached Done within the MTD window. QA testing time logged directly on the parent ticket (no sub-ticket) is not captured here. This run found one candidate sub-ticket (MAIN-9312: MAIN-6275 | QA, logged by Nherissa Dagal), but its parent (MAIN-6275) had not reached Done as of this run, so it does not qualify — hence zero rows above.","rows":[]},"raw":{"headers":["Day","User","Ticket","Hours"],"rows":[["09/08","Adam Koehler","FL-736","4"],["09/08","Adam Koehler","MAIN-5148","2"],["09/08","Adam Koehler","MAIN-9198","1"],["09/08","Alec Patterson","MM-179","1"],["09/08","Alec Patter